WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
1. Bill comparison. Check the dates before comparing the amounts.

00:01.000 --> 00:05.000
2. Product charges. GPU hours, rates, and line items explain a product charge.

00:05.000 --> 00:09.000
3. Usage totals. Token counts describe consumption, not dollars.

00:09.000 --> 00:13.000
4. Traffic and performance. These charts show how the service performed, not its dollar cost.

00:13.000 --> 00:17.000
5. Request logs. Inspect what ran: the model, token counts, status, and timing.

00:17.000 --> 00:21.000
6. Account activity. Model and endpoint updates are clues to investigate, not proof of a cause.
